 "readme": "# Project Overview\n\n## Environment Setup\n\n1. Install dependencies:\n    ```bash\n    conda env create -f environment.yml\n    ```\n\n## Main Directory Description\n\n- `data/`: Stores datasets and preprocessing scripts.\n- `models/`: Contains model definitions and related code.\n- `models_info`: Stores trained target models.\n- `utils/`: Utility functions and helper scripts.\n- `results/`: Experimental validation results.\n- `config/`: Configuration files (e.g., hyperparameter settings).\n- `core`: Core algorithms of this method.\n- `search` and `train`: Outer wrapper classes and related functions.\n- `plausible`: Methods related to box/unit partitioning.\n- `labeling`: Code for discrimination detection functions.\n- `evaluation`: Code for evaluation experiments.\n- `baseline`: Contains baseline models.\n- `limictgan`: Dependency algorithm library for the LIMI method.\n- `logs`: Runtime and error logs.\n- `baseline`: Contains baseline methods. Before running, add the current file path to the system path so dependencies can be resolved.\n\n## Main Python Test Files and Shell Scripts\n\n- `run_train.sh`: One-click training script for the SDF+DIR model.\n- `run_search.sh`: One-click script to run the proposed method.\n\n- `compare_ID_Rate.py`: Tests individual fairness metrics of models.\n- `coverage_eval.py`: Tests the similarity between the modeled data domain and the real data domain.\n- `compare_performance_eval.py`: Performance comparison against baseline models.\n- `compare_coverage_eval.py`: Coverage (diversity) comparison against baseline models.\n- `audit_record.py`: Audit records for fairness testing.",
